#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124213 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124650 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf44a846-8458-5e2f-bef3-72cf87a6035f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intercepts of a Hyperboloid"}] :question/id #uuid "58966f53-5f83-5c86-8ffe-38ad0dffd2b3" :question/math-academy-id "e-12555" :question/problem "Given the hyperboloid of one sheet  $\\dfrac{(x-3)^2}9 + \\dfrac{(y+4)^2}{16} - \\dfrac{(z-5)^2}{25} = 1,$ find its intercepts with the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "To find the $x$-intercepts, we plug $y=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(0+4)^{2}}{16}-\\frac{(0-5)^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9}+1-1 & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =9 \\\\ x-3 & =\\pm \\sqrt{9} \\\\ x & =3\\pm 3 \\\\ x & =0,6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $x$-axis are $(0,0,0)$ and $(6,0,0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124312 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124503 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b079a5ff-e73a-592f-b16c-8740682538f3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Domain of a Hyperboloid"}] :question/id #uuid "e85cfe0b-4ff6-5cce-9384-aeb930843b49" :question/math-academy-id "e-5265" :question/problem "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets $(x-1)^2 + y^2 - \\dfrac{z^2}{4} = -1,$ find the domain of $z = z(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "From the hyperboloid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4} & =-1 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2}+1 & =\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4} & =(x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2}+1 \\\\ {z}^{2} & =4((x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2}+1) \\\\ z & =\\pm 2\\sqrt{(x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe square root is defined only for non-negative arguments. However, notice that for all $(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2,$ we have\n\n$$\n(x-1)^2 + y^2 + 1 \\geq 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $z(x,y)$ is $\\mathbb R^2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124364 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124555 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d28eda1a-a90b-57e9-969a-eb36552e413e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Traces of Hyperboloids"}] :question/id #uuid "1fbe37ed-9022-5c44-851c-0e66fe2fb79f" :question/math-academy-id "e-6078" :question/problem "The projection of the intersection between the hyperboloid of two sheets \n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{(x-5)^2}{8} + \\dfrac{y^2}{50} + (z-3)^2 = -1\n$$\n\nand the plane $z = 4$ onto the $xy$-plane is a hyperbola. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the hyperbola?" :question/worked-solution "To find the intersection of the hyperboloid and the plane $z = 4,$ we substitute $z = 4$ into the equation of the hyperboloid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{50}+(z-3)^{2} & =-1 \\\\ -\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{50}+1=-1 \\\\ -\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{50} & =-2 \\\\ \\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{50} & =2 \\\\ \\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{100} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{{4}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{10}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbola with semi-axes of lengths $4$ and $10.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124825 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124503 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b079a5ff-e73a-592f-b16c-8740682538f3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Domain of a Hyperboloid"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a262ffc-6506-5c9e-bd4d-cdabbb9049f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282735} {:answer/id #uuid "7a7fd666-f923-5f81-ae78-497f0ff2f5f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282739} {:answer/id #uuid "96a36656-5f13-584b-a2c1-60487a050d9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282994} {:answer/id #uuid "dc689ac7-1d1e-5af3-a982-f296478da3a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283613} {:answer/id #uuid "ef74907b-ee99-5ac1-904e-c87df8af5bfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef74907b-ee99-5ac1-904e-c87df8af5bfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283775} :answer-field/id #uuid "b588b8e6-df0e-5564-96f7-a63dd0c60df7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284252}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2cb27705-2ef7-5315-a2e6-466639501b52" :question/math-academy-id "q-164232" :question/problem "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}=-1$, find the domain of $z=z(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "From the hyperboloid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2} & =-1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1 & ={z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{2} & =1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} \\\\ {z}^{2} & =\\pm \\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe square root is defined only for non-negative arguments. However, notice that for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $z(x,y)$ is ${R}^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124827 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124650 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf44a846-8458-5e2f-bef3-72cf87a6035f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intercepts of a Hyperboloid"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d17af416-0b3a-53e9-b003-ea9afeff57b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(1, 0, 0)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121560} {:answer/id #uuid "ee394826-68a0-5d4d-8fad-b3acff19172c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-1, 0, 0)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121561} {:answer/id #uuid "15ac2938-5138-5e3b-b237-6438822be2cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-1, 0, 0)$ and $(1, 0, 0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121562} {:answer/id #uuid "2d7f6298-95f3-55b3-ad96-de0f1459e991" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0, 0, 0)$ and $(1, 0, 0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121563} {:answer/id #uuid "500b4af2-6965-582f-93c4-d89ecd9277b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The hyperboloid does not intersect the $x$-axis." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121564}] :answer-field/id #uuid "8d40a13e-a03d-5915-b8f0-6a868d9dec93" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121559}] :question/id #uuid "737faeb3-a7eb-5493-ac19-bfe35360ff79" :question/math-academy-id "q-164234" :question/problem "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets $x^{2} + y^{2} - z^{2} =-1$, find its $x$-intercepts."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378906 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124650 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf44a846-8458-5e2f-bef3-72cf87a6035f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intercepts of a Hyperboloid"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d01ecc7e-5e60-5e00-82e2-a3560578ba8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,5)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378908} {:answer/id #uuid "1b553d47-4ec0-54f1-84b3-2f1f8ab68995" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,-5\\sqrt{2})$ and $(0,0,5\\sqrt{2})$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378909} {:answer/id #uuid "50374b0f-33cf-56ef-8e00-8a80f4a9e261" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,-2)$ and $(0,0,2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378910} {:answer/id #uuid "fa6edcce-081c-524c-ae8d-dacf3d742a86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,5\\sqrt{2})$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378911} {:answer/id #uuid "1fe86808-a860-5dea-a76d-b7863ec75224" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The hyperboloid does not intersect the $z$-axis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378912}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b553d47-4ec0-54f1-84b3-2f1f8ab68995" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,-5\\sqrt{2})$ and $(0,0,5\\sqrt{2})$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378909} :answer-field/id #uuid "0532ee3e-209b-5f25-a2ee-3ab81c7de490" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378907}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c22c6a7b-1fb3-5e18-82c2-bb58ebb939fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-164274" :question/problem "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets $\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+{y}^{2}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{25}=-1,$ find its $z$-intercepts." :question/worked-solution "To find the $z$-intercepts, we plug $x=0$ and $y=0$ into the equation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(0-2)^{2}}{4}+{0}^{2}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{25} & =-1 \\\\ 1-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{25} & =-1 \\\\ -\\frac{{z}^{2}}{25} & =-2 \\\\ {z}^{2} & =50 \\\\ z & =\\pm 5\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $z=-5\\sqrt{2}$ and $z=5\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $z$-axis are $(0,0,-5\\sqrt{2})$ and $(0,0,5\\sqrt{2}).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284466 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124650 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf44a846-8458-5e2f-bef3-72cf87a6035f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intercepts of a Hyperboloid"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08b9352f-5f16-5022-b582-83d9d8a8365f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,-6+\\sqrt{5},0)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281765} {:answer/id #uuid "2e45c792-da28-56f2-a59e-cf1b6162c371" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,-6+\\sqrt{5},0)$ and $(0,-6-\\sqrt{5},0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282097} {:answer/id #uuid "4c849fdb-0521-51cd-a8e6-4865ca952411" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,-6,0)$  only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282345} {:answer/id #uuid "b08021fc-edb5-5bd8-872e-2b9809587bb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The hyperboloid does not intersect the $y$-axis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283215} {:answer/id #uuid "ec64f8da-e4af-533c-98e9-228575539e00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,-3,0)$ and $(0,3,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283758}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b08021fc-edb5-5bd8-872e-2b9809587bb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The hyperboloid does not intersect the $y$-axis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283215} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7955c55-9605-5ab6-9b1f-775ef239ceb3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284225}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "87f4b219-b4ca-56b4-a84e-4618201b700e" :question/math-academy-id "q-164284" :question/problem "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets $\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(y+6)^{2}}{5}-(z-1)^{2}=-1,$ find its $y$-intercepts." :question/worked-solution "To find the $y$-intercepts, we plug $x=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(0+3)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(y+6)^{2}}{5}-(0-1)^{2} & =-1 \\\\ 3+\\frac{(y+6)^{2}}{5}-1 & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{(y+6)^{2}}{5} & =-3 \\\\ (y+6)^{2} & =-15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation has no (real) solutions.\n\nTherefore, the hyperboloid does not intersect the $y$-axis."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408096 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124503 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b079a5ff-e73a-592f-b16c-8740682538f3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Domain of a Hyperboloid"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1947e7ad-9f28-5f1c-bbd7-0534d7ae56a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}>1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408083} {:answer/id #uuid "4a717d1f-b7eb-5705-90ee-dc90eea2ac01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}\\ge 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408084} {:answer/id #uuid "69b1c641-c4ea-5e70-b0c0-21d7aa7137c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}\\le 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408087} {:answer/id #uuid "cd42f6f5-8e5b-53dc-b5eb-fcddd900ecf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408089} {:answer/id #uuid "fda21d60-b280-5d0d-beed-f16249e1a048" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}<1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408092}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd42f6f5-8e5b-53dc-b5eb-fcddd900ecf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408089} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e07a855-54d3-5672-a263-c28fae61891d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408093}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "28ec3dc9-c6d5-5b75-a09b-0f48f395ab8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-164302" :question/problem "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets $(x+1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{9}=-1,$ find the domain of $z=z(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "From the hyperboloid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{9} & =-1 \\\\ (x+1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}+1 & =\\frac{{z}^{2}}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{z}^{2}}{9} & =(x+1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}+1 \\\\ {z}^{2} & =9((x+1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}+1) \\\\ z & =\\pm 3\\sqrt{(x+1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe square root is defined only for non-negative arguments. However, notice that for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n(x+1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}+1\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $z(x,y)$ is ${R}^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378920 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124503 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b079a5ff-e73a-592f-b16c-8740682538f3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Domain of a Hyperboloid"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01af6213-439b-5eac-b318-f7cb7633b916" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{2}+{y}^{2}<1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378922} {:answer/id #uuid "2f6824e3-a031-5289-8272-ac90c0afa561" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378923} {:answer/id #uuid "5f615af2-d250-50af-bde8-eeeacad53e13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378924} {:answer/id #uuid "c320d8c6-f3c0-5c3f-a7a2-639ce24f8db3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378925} {:answer/id #uuid "051cf573-4468-506a-b756-2e919742a9f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{2}+{y}^{2}>1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378926}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f6824e3-a031-5289-8272-ac90c0afa561" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378923} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac94e8ec-04ff-5e98-9898-11795c26f50b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378921}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "62c4e3bb-f437-5cc4-9639-1ab5e45aee0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-164304" :question/problem "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets $\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{2}+{y}^{2}-(z+2)^{2}=-1,$ find the domain of $z=z(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "From the hyperboloid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{2}+{y}^{2}-(z+2)^{2} & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{2}+{y}^{2}+1 & =(z+2)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(z+2)^{2} & =\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{2}+{y}^{2}+1 \\\\ z+2 & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{2}+{y}^{2}+1} \\\\ z & =-2\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{2}+{y}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe square root is defined only for non-negative arguments. However, notice that for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{2}+{y}^{2}+1\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $z(x,y)$ is ${R}^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284469 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124503 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b079a5ff-e73a-592f-b16c-8740682538f3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Domain of a Hyperboloid"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28dfc208-68c2-5f88-8bd4-209d53beb5ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282042} {:answer/id #uuid "36789465-716b-57b5-bcb5-c61d70e72a4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 3\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487670} {:answer/id #uuid "389cbac5-a671-5c39-a922-51617d9c06fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}>1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487674} {:answer/id #uuid "639e7663-1b18-512b-aaa1-be4700f6151a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487764} {:answer/id #uuid "c59c6bc5-e7d5-524f-b87d-e788fbdad7bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}<3\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487943}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "639e7663-1b18-512b-aaa1-be4700f6151a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487764} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ac34746-de0d-5226-892a-e787c1d531e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283953}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cc95e142-b514-5431-9924-bdc1db9331dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-164307" :question/problem "Given the hyperboloid of one sheet $(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}-(z-3)^{2}=1,$ find the domain of $z=z(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "From the hyperboloid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}-(z-3)^{2} & =1 \\\\ (x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}-1 & =(z-3)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(z-3)^{2} & =(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}-1 \\\\ z-3 & =\\pm \\sqrt{(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}-1} \\\\ z & =3\\pm \\sqrt{(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the square root is defined only for non-negative arguments, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}-1 & \\ge 0 \\\\ (x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2} & \\ge 1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the exterior of the circle $(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}=1,$ which includes the boundary.\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 1\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284478 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124555 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d28eda1a-a90b-57e9-969a-eb36552e413e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Traces of Hyperboloids"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "118b88a3-dc3c-5b2b-b0a3-3478959777a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$ and $6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281854} {:answer/id #uuid "2a108e8b-bd90-5bee-afc2-e1d24910cc47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$9$ and $36$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282053} {:answer/id #uuid "9cb060fa-13b0-544d-8016-5c8ee5b31427" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{3}$ and $\\sqrt{6}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283055} {:answer/id #uuid "ab442a50-e271-5517-885a-f3571c085a58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{3}$ and $2\\sqrt{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283173} {:answer/id #uuid "daa26f47-47cd-5712-a9fb-e6a642df1dee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$ and $12$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283596}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "118b88a3-dc3c-5b2b-b0a3-3478959777a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$ and $6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281854} :answer-field/id #uuid "427d6dbf-8269-54f4-8cb2-2973908eeebd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284041}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dffb042f-0149-507c-b07f-f0b0026b0640" :question/math-academy-id "q-164379" :question/problem "The projection of the intersection between the hyperboloid of two sheets ${x}^{2}-\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(z+3)^{2}}{12}=-1$ and the plane $x=\\sqrt{2}$ onto the $yz$-plane is a hyperbola. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the hyperbola?" :question/worked-solution "To find the intersection of the hyperboloid and the plane $x=\\sqrt{2},$ we substitute $x=\\sqrt{2}$ into the equation of the hyperboloid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\sqrt{2})^{2}-\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(z+3)^{2}}{12} & =-1 \\\\ 2-\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(z+3)^{2}}{12} & =-1 \\\\ -\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(z+3)^{2}}{12} & =-3 \\\\ \\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{3}-\\frac{(z+3)^{2}}{12} & =3 \\\\ \\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{(z+3)^{2}}{36} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}-\\frac{(z+3)^{2}}{{6}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbola with semi-axes of lengths $3$ and $6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124883 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124650 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf44a846-8458-5e2f-bef3-72cf87a6035f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intercepts of a Hyperboloid"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b775388f-c205-5231-955c-1be8cc45a77d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(2, 0, 0)$ and $(4, 0, 0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121899} {:answer/id #uuid "2cba7e56-4010-5664-a1e4-8e6839a9237d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(2, 0, 0)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121900} {:answer/id #uuid "5dd05e7c-03b5-5297-b143-3b79c9ccc7b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0, 0, 0)$ and $(4, 0, 0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121901} {:answer/id #uuid "6ebba00d-4b6e-5cad-bb23-aa227ca72dc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0, 0, 0)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121902} {:answer/id #uuid "76f4d9a7-c1de-58f5-be04-bddf06eb6b66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-2, 0, 0)$ and $(2, 0, 0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121903}] :answer-field/id #uuid "d301b3cc-68d1-56cf-af21-197e877899e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121898} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3e1ac47-360d-5d4e-81d1-77973106ffce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(2,0,0)$ and $(4,0,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402416} {:answer/id #uuid "d9cbb92f-a748-575a-a28c-ccd51fd2a063" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-2,0,0)$ and $(2,0,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402417} {:answer/id #uuid "a0eac9ba-097c-562d-b7e8-c5b232de791f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,0)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402418} {:answer/id #uuid "e713d157-180a-577c-a9f9-9ff6ffb97431" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(2,0,0)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402419} {:answer/id #uuid "a32d291b-ec75-560e-9073-c1604179fc76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,0)$ and $(4,0,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402420}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a32d291b-ec75-560e-9073-c1604179fc76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,0)$ and $(4,0,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402420} :answer-field/id #uuid "8cad8bb9-4c82-52b7-8b49-6c5af6fbba05" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402415}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "49b0818a-b11e-5262-8180-2b40dd5a4460" :question/math-academy-id "q-35429" :question/problem "Given the hyperboloid of one sheet $\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{5}=1$, find its $x$-intercepts." :question/worked-solution "To find the $x$-intercepts, we plug $y=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{0}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{5} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =4 \\\\ x-2 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ x & =2\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $x=0$ and $x=4.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $x$-axis are $(0,0,0)$ and $(4,0,0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323801 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124503 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b079a5ff-e73a-592f-b16c-8740682538f3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Domain of a Hyperboloid"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16b247dd-fec8-5ca0-973c-2e5283ca38cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}<0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321333} {:answer/id #uuid "61eca7e5-5fa6-5690-a884-1b0e9b6596f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The entire $xy$-plane" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321913} {:answer/id #uuid "90c09e40-2729-5ade-8409-6290b0249236" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}<1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322296} {:answer/id #uuid "adcd90b4-3530-55e6-af62-f4a55da2ba2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}\\ge 0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322511} {:answer/id #uuid "f8c6cf8c-9492-52a4-b891-983ac582c05c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}\\ge 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323104}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8c6cf8c-9492-52a4-b891-983ac582c05c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}\\ge 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323104} :answer-field/id #uuid "787e8934-c73f-50c0-b941-8b2a7ad64fd6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323405}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e7388c8d-bcb0-58d2-b80f-408abd20ed3a" :question/math-academy-id "q-36388" :question/problem "Given the hyperboloid of one sheet  $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{3}=1$, find the domain of $z=z(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "From the hyperboloid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{3} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}-1 & =\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{3} \\\\ (z+1)^{2} & =3(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}-1) \\\\ (z+1) & =\\pm \\sqrt{3(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}-1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince the square root is defined only for non-negative arguments, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}-1 & \\ge 0 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & \\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the exterior of the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=1$, including its boundary.\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}\\ge 1}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339024 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124555 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d28eda1a-a90b-57e9-969a-eb36552e413e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Traces of Hyperboloids"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "814b4a42-b7cd-5c96-abc1-fcc5fdad2c79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337205} {:answer/id #uuid "8d468010-79df-59bd-872e-d3fd01c81e85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337309} {:answer/id #uuid "a78c2605-56b5-5696-b9c8-72124ebef4a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337547} {:answer/id #uuid "c0bdc080-f8a2-5e4e-b062-563f8bd39807" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337743} {:answer/id #uuid "f25d7c87-0431-5885-9744-ce33cd1af3ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338153}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0bdc080-f8a2-5e4e-b062-563f8bd39807" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337743} :answer-field/id #uuid "b938efa7-bc21-5de4-8979-73eee0896912" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338614}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5245b647-c0fc-5986-8420-2ef311981e4b" :question/math-academy-id "q-71957" :question/problem "What is the trace in the $xy$-plane of the hyperboloid of one sheet $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{6}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the trace in the $xy$-plane, we substitute $z=0$ into the equation of the hyperboloid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{0}^{2}}{6}=1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbola in $xy$-plane."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380015 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124555 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d28eda1a-a90b-57e9-969a-eb36552e413e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Traces of Hyperboloids"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07be1d92-3207-5844-8363-47e8beb1dae0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{8}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380017} {:answer/id #uuid "874ff040-8380-53ca-8723-f3687b5d9807" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380018} {:answer/id #uuid "b424a8d6-7f90-56a5-a346-193fa3abade6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380019} {:answer/id #uuid "c1ed6cfd-a655-5d76-9c9d-448f6084d215" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{8}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380020} {:answer/id #uuid "ebd91678-4079-58df-9686-6ccf2e85dd53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{8}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380021}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ebd91678-4079-58df-9686-6ccf2e85dd53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{8}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380021} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b8c86f9-7db1-52bc-859b-d608ce2b3140" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380016}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c19a1ca0-bd04-523a-8ce1-ec11d04df921" :question/math-academy-id "q-74022" :question/problem "What is the trace in the $xz$-plane of the hyperboloid of one sheet $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{8}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the trace in the $xz$-plane, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the hyperboloid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{5}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{8}=1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{8}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of the ellipse in $xy$-plane."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380022 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124555 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d28eda1a-a90b-57e9-969a-eb36552e413e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Traces of Hyperboloids"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e06071b-7f63-5370-9aa4-6e3d2ae0f7f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ and $5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380024} {:answer/id #uuid "ceefef73-e49d-5607-b222-3ee1c5ed4b12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{5}$ and $4\\sqrt{5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380025} {:answer/id #uuid "cddedb39-a1e1-55bb-8ae3-3e2356793dce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$10$ and $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380026} {:answer/id #uuid "b5cdd6b1-ad00-5eee-9a26-e87327f21ceb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{5}$ and $5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380027} {:answer/id #uuid "c3ba4a65-4280-51a1-a086-298fbc98f01a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$10$ and $5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380028}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3ba4a65-4280-51a1-a086-298fbc98f01a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$10$ and $5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380028} :answer-field/id #uuid "0907267b-b9e7-57b7-9485-3ee41b06f7d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380023}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e2030444-4bd3-5c60-8670-ebaeefcce4d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-74024" :question/problem "The projection of the intersection between the hyperboloid of two sheets $\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{20}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{80}=-1$ and the plane $y=4$ onto the $xz$-plane is a hyperbola. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the hyperbola?" :question/worked-solution "To find the intersection of the hyperboloid and the plane $y=4$, we substitute $y=4$ into the equation of the hyperboloid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{20}+\\frac{(4-2)^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{80} & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{20}+\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{80} & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{20}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{80} & =-1-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{20}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{80} & =-\\frac{5}{4} \\\\ -\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{100} & =1 \\\\ -\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{{5}^{2}}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{10}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbola with semi-axes of lengths $10$ and $5.$"}]}
